{"name":"Ranch Acres","hex":"#f3e7cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ranch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large plot of land used for raising cattle, sheep or other livestock.","A small farm that cultivates vegetables or livestock, especially one in the Southwestern United States."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To operate a ranch; to engage in ranching.","To work on a ranch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch"},{"term":"acres","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of acre"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acres"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ranch","blocks":[{"text":"A ranch is an area of land, including various structures, given primarily to ranching, the practice of raising grazing livestock such as cattle and sheep. It is a subtype of farm. These terms are most often applied to livestock-raising operations in Mexico, the Western United States and Western Canada, though there are ranches in other areas. People who own or operate a ranch are called ranchers, cattlemen, or stockgrowers. Ranching is also a method used to raise less common livestock such as horses, elk, American bison, ostrich, emu, and alpaca."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg/330px-Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranch"},{"title":"Acre","blocks":[{"text":"The acre is a unit of land area used in the British imperial and the United States customary systems. It is traditionally defined as the area of one chain by one furlong, which is exactly equal to 10 square chains, 1⁄640 of a square mile, 4,840 square yards, or 43,560 square feet, and approximately 4,047 m2, or about 40% of a hectare. The acre is sometimes abbreviated ac, but is usually spelled out as the word \"acre\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Acre_superimposed_over_football_fields.svg/330px-Acre_superimposed_over_football_fields.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acre"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/1280px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Principales_vias_pecuarias.png/500px-Principales_vias_pecuarias.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Principales_vias_pecuarias.png/500px-Principales_vias_pecuarias.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Main transhumance routes in Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrincipales_vias_pecuarias.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg/500px-Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg/500px-Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"